@page "/terms"
@layout MarketingLayout

<HeadContent>
    <SeoHeadContent Path="/terms"
                    Title="Terms of Service — Brainy"
                    Description="The terms that govern using Brainy: acceptable use, account responsibilities, billing, liability, and termination." />
</HeadContent>

<section class="mkt-hero">
    <div class="mkt-wrap">
        <span class="mkt-eyebrow mkt-rise">Trust</span>
        <h1 class="mkt-title mkt-rise mkt-d1" style="max-width: 16em; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem);">
            Terms of Service
        </h1>
        <p class="mkt-lead mkt-rise mkt-d2" style="margin-top: 1.1rem;">
            The terms that govern using Brainy, in plain language.
        </p>
        <div class="mkt-draft-notice mkt-rise mkt-d3" role="note">
            <span class="mkt-draft-notice__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;&#65039;</span>
            <p>
                <strong>Draft &mdash; pending qualified legal review.</strong> These terms are product
                documentation describing intended terms of use. They are not a finalized legal agreement and have
                not yet been reviewed by qualified legal counsel for your jurisdiction.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mkt-section">
    <div class="mkt-wrap">
        <article class="mkt-changelog">

            <h2>Accepting these terms</h2>
            <p>
                By creating a Brainy account or otherwise using Brainy, you agree to these Terms of Service and to
                the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>,
                which are incorporated here by reference.
            </p>

            <h2>Your account</h2>
            <p>
                You are responsible for the accuracy of your account information, for keeping your password
                confidential, and for all activity that happens under your account. Tell us promptly if you
                believe your account has been compromised. Brainy requires a password and, for destructive actions
                such as account deletion, an exact typed confirmation phrase &mdash; treat both as sensitive.
            </p>

            <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
            <p>
                Your use of Brainy must comply with the <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>.
                Violating it may result in suspension or termination of your account.
            </p>

            <h2>Your content</h2>
            <p>
                You own the notes, tasks, projects and other content you create in Brainy ("your content"). You
                grant Brainy only the limited rights needed to store, process, and display your content back to
                you, and &mdash; solely when you explicitly trigger an AI feature and the deployment has AI
                enabled &mdash; to send the relevant portion of your content to the configured AI provider as
                described in <a href="/ai-transparency">AI &amp; Your Data</a>. Your content is never used to
                train Brainy's or any subprocessor's models.
            </p>

            <h2>AI-generated content</h2>
            <p>
                Some features let Brainy generate suggestions, summaries, action items or draft output using AI.
                AI-generated content can be incorrect or incomplete. It is always labeled as AI-generated, always
                retains the model and prompt version used, and always preserves your original content and source
                references separately so you can review before relying on it. You are responsible for reviewing
                AI-generated content before acting on it.
            </p>

            <h2>Plans and billing</h2>
            <p>
                Brainy's current plans, pricing, and what happens if you downgrade are described on the
                <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a> page, which forms part of these terms for the plan you select.
                Billing details, invoicing, and payment processing are handled separately from this document.
            </p>

            <h2>Service availability</h2>
            <p>
                Brainy is provided on an "as available" basis. We aim for reliable service but do not guarantee
                uninterrupted or error-free operation.
            </p>

            <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
            <p>
                To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Brainy and its operators are not liable for
                indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of the service. Nothing in
                these terms limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable law. This section, like the
                rest of this page, is a draft placeholder pending qualified legal review for your jurisdiction.
            </p>

            <h2>Termination</h2>
            <p>
                You may stop using Brainy and delete your account at any time from
                <a href="/Account/Manage">Account and data</a>. We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate
                the <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a> or these terms. On termination, your right
                to use Brainy ends; your data is handled as described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
            <p>
                Brainy may update these terms as the product evolves. Material changes will be reflected on this
                page, and continued use after an update constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
            </p>

        </article>
    </div>
</section>
